{
  "_comment": "Forum wallet-login wire contract between warren-connect (the DiscourseConnect broker) and every Warren client, frozen at v1: the X-Warren signing inputs and the exact signed request bytes for a login and for an in-app report, plus the provider's canonical answer per outcome. Synthetic host, key and secret only. The signing rule itself (canonical message, SS58 address) is pinned by identity.json; this file pins what rides on it for the forum routes. Adding a request name here breaks the consumers until they handle it, on purpose.",
  "version": 1,
  "signer": {
    "_comment": "signing_key_hex is the raw 32-byte Ed25519 secret (SigningKey::from_bytes), not a wallet seed: identity.json pins the seed-to-key derivation. timestamp is the X-Warren-Timestamp value; the provider accepts it within 60 seconds of its own clock, so these exact bytes replayed through a live provider land on the clock_skew answer, and their acceptance is proven by verifying with the provider clock set to timestamp. connect_host is not signed (only the path is) and stands in for the deployment's connect host.",
    "signing_key_hex": "1111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111",
